From dc27600fb7360f3bb4be03ff8685ef6e4d1cea26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:11:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(accounting): month-end accrual for recurring
 expenses via Accounts Payable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Recurring expenses can now opt into month-end provisioning: on the last day
of the month, a nightly job books an accrual (DR Expense / CR 2004 Accounts
Payable) for any active monthly recurring expense that hasn't actually been
recorded yet that period. Once the real bill is approved, the accrual is
automatically reversed against the same vendor's payable card instead of
double-booking the expense, with any variance between the estimated and
actual amount adjusted through the expense account.

2004 posts against the specific vendor's own sub-ledger, finishing the
Vendor business-partner control-account wiring that already existed for
Dues Receivable but was never linked up — auto_provision now requires a
vendor for exactly this reason. Also fixes a latent gap where approved
recurring expenses were never posted to the ledger at all.

Adds a Recurring Expenses page (vendor picker, provisioning toggle,
accrual review list) and a GET /expenses/provisions endpoint.
